{"kind":"assert","text":"Connected browser story review-policy handoff clarification, grounded in fresh adopted R2r15 reads atf4889d47 section7.1/10.3/18.5 and adopted R3r28 at8b1c3c9 sections3.10/12.1.4a/12.1.5 extent judgment. Existing designs already distinguish these; this is not a defect, new protocol choice or source commission. Initial create/import/review UI and I6/N6 walkthrough must state the actual declared review policy rather than infer counted eligibility from an agent having a different member identity.\nA and returning B are devices of ONE member; two keys are one reviewer. A person who only controls an independently signing agent may give its counted ordinary review when ownerMayReview is true and all other qualification requirements hold. When ownerMayReview is false, the lane may record that person's verdict while the destination does not count it. Either way a selected contributor, integrator, holder under a selected commitment, or retained principal in the manifest authors cannot supply the counted review; another device of that member changes nothing. Initial policy must be visible and explicit. Do not silently enable ownerMayReview to make a scripted journey pass; use the selected declared policy or another qualified independent member.\nFor the rules extent, ownerMayReview is treated as false and a counted reviewer must hold rules.publish with required independence. The declared singleControllerException is a separate reservation judgment, not permission for counted self-review: declaration, exactly one current active controller with active key, and the author/controller conflict condition must all be evidenced under current R28. Checks and merger authority remain. A page shows it as declared/pending judgment and says used only from the recorded reservation outcome. Source/infra review eligibility does not automatically satisfy rules review.\nRetarget the historical005 human-review expectation through these current R2/R3 rules. Meaningful integrated acceptance reuses existing I5/I6/R4 owners: (a) controlled agent contribution only, ownerMayReview=true, qualified returningB recorded/countable; (b) same contribution with ownerMayReview=false, B's recorded verdict does not meet publication and a qualified C does; (c) B's member contributed/integrated, no device or owner flag bypass; include rules-extent judgment/declared exception in its existing witness. This is a compact policy/identity boundary, not another full browser suite or first-Jam gate. UI distinguishes activity, review recorded, eligibility under observed policy, destination reservation and final publication; provisional/client counts cannot replace the latter outcomes. Full browser/provider/IA/source/qualification evidence remains owed; root ran no test or project code.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","owner":"existing I5/I6/R4/N6 handoff; planner efc reconciliation"}}